hist:'A major Mesopotamian city from the early 2nd millennium BC. Under Nebuchadnezzar II (605–562 BC) it was rebuilt with the Ishtar Gate, the Processional Way and the ziggurat Etemenanki. Cyrus of Persia took it in 539 BC. Robert Koldewey excavated it from 1899 to 1917.',
bib:'The tower of Babel. Babylon conquers Judah, Jehoiachin and Daniel are taken there, and the exiles weep by its rivers. Belshazzar\'s feast and the fall of the city appear in Daniel 5.',
civ:[['Old Babylonian (Hammurabi)',-1894,-1595],['Kassite',-1595,-1155],['Assyrian domination',-900,-626],['Neo-Babylonian',-626,-539],['Persian',-539,-331],['Hellenistic',-331,-141]],
vis:'Reconstructed walls and the Ishtar Gate replica on site, excavated foundations of Nebuchadnezzar\'s palaces, the base of Etemenanki, and the Lion of Babylon. The original Ishtar Gate is in the Pergamon Museum, Berlin. UNESCO World Heritage since 2019.',
v:[['Genesis 11:9','The city is called Babel because the LORD confused the language.'],['2 Kings 24:10-16','Nebuchadnezzar besieges Jerusalem and carries Jehoiachin to Babylon.'],['2 Kings 25:27-30','Evil-Merodach releases Jehoiachin and gives him a regular allowance.'],['Psalm 137:1','"By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down and wept."'],['Daniel 4:30','Nebuchadnezzar boasts of "great Babylon, which I have built".'],['Daniel 5:30-31','Belshazzar is killed and Darius the Mede receives the kingdom.'],['Ezra 1:1-3','Cyrus decrees that the Temple may be rebuilt.']],
tl:[[-1754,'c. 1754 BC','Hammurabi\'s law code.','h'],[-605,'605 BC','Nebuchadnezzar II becomes king; Daniel taken to Babylon.','b'],[-597,'597 BC','Jehoiachin deported to Babylon.','b'],[-586,'587/586 BC','Jerusalem destroyed; mass deportation.','b'],[-562,'c. 562 BC','Jehoiachin released by Amel-Marduk (Evil-Merodach).','b'],[-539,'539 BC','Cyrus takes Babylon.','h'],[-323,'323 BC','Alexander the Great dies in Babylon.','h'],[1899,'1899–1917','Robert Koldewey excavates for the German Oriental Society.','x'],[2019,'2019','Inscribed as UNESCO World Heritage.','x']],
