sum:'Third city of the Roman Empire and base of the first mission to the Gentiles; the disciples were first called Christians here.',
hist:'Founded about 300 BC by Seleucus I and capital of the Seleucid kingdom, then of Roman Syria. Princeton excavations (1932–39) recovered many Roman mosaics, now in the Hatay Archaeology Museum. The modern city was severely damaged in the February 2023 earthquakes.',
bib:'Believers scattered after Stephen\'s death preach to Greeks. Barnabas and Paul teach here, and the church sends Paul on all three missionary journeys.',
