sum:'The largest Canaanite city in the land, "the head of all those kingdoms" according to Joshua 11.',
hist:'In the Middle and Late Bronze Ages Hazor covered about 80 hectares and is mentioned in Egyptian and Mari texts. A violent destruction by fire ended the Late Bronze city in the 13th century BC. An Iron Age Israelite city followed, with a six-chambered gate and a large water system.',
bib:'Joshua defeats Jabin, king of Hazor, and burns the city. Another Jabin of Hazor oppresses Israel in Judges 4. Solomon fortifies Hazor, and Tiglath-Pileser III captures it.',
