lat:32.5847,lon:35.1847,pr:'certain',ty:'City / mound',cat:['ot','nt','israel'],wiki:'Tel Megiddo',
sum:'A strategic fortress city guarding the Via Maris pass, scene of many battles, and the source of the name "Armageddon".',
hist:'Megiddo has about 20 occupation levels from the Neolithic to the Persian period. Thutmose III besieged it about 1457 BC (the first battle recorded in detail). Iron Age layers include gates, stables or storehouses and a water system. Excavations: Schumacher (1903–05), the University of Chicago (1925–39), Yadin (1960s) and Tel Aviv University (1992–2022).',
bib:'Joshua defeats its king. Deborah\'s song mentions "the waters of Megiddo". Solomon fortifies it, Ahaziah and Josiah die here, and Revelation names Armageddon.',
civ:[['Canaanite city-state',-3000,-1150],['Egyptian control',-1457,-1150],['Israelite',-1000,-732],['Assyrian province',-732,-600],['Persian',-539,-332]],
vis:'The excavated mound with its city gates, Canaanite temples and "round altar", the pillared buildings and the Iron Age water tunnel (Tel Megiddo, part of the UNESCO "Biblical Tels" listing).',
v:[['Joshua 12:21','The king of Megiddo is listed among the defeated kings.'],['Judges 5:19','The kings of Canaan fight "by the waters of Megiddo".'],['1 Kings 9:15','Solomon builds Megiddo.'],['2 Kings 9:27','Ahaziah flees to Megiddo and dies there.'],['2 Kings 23:29-30','Josiah is killed at Megiddo by Pharaoh Necho.'],['Revelation 16:16','The kings gather at Har-Magedon.']],
