sum:'Between Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal; where Abram first built an altar in Canaan and Joshua renewed the covenant.',
hist:'A major Middle Bronze Age city with massive walls, gates and a large fortress-temple. It appears in Egyptian execration texts and the Amarna letters (under Labayu). It was briefly the first capital of the northern kingdom.',
bib:'God promises the land to Abram here. Jacob buys land here, Joseph\'s bones are buried here, Joshua renews the covenant, Abimelech destroys the tower of Shechem, and Rehoboam is rejected here.',
